course: dictionary
lesson: 3
title: Animal words in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An aardwolf is a small striped animal from southern and eastern Africa. You can work out what it is from the words around it: «the aardwolf is a small hyena that eats mostly termites». Small, hyena and eats tell you it is an animal, not a plant or a machine.
explain: Ask yourself: what kind of thing fits in this sentence? The clue «eats mostly termites» tells you what it eats. Then swap in your meaning, an animal that eats termites, and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Science lessons use this word when they talk about food chains and adaptation. Each night an aardwolf licks up thousands of termites with its long sticky tongue. That tongue is a body part that helps it survive, so it is an adaptation for catching termites.
fact: An aardwolf is a small striped animal of southern and eastern Africa.
fact: The aardwolf is related to the hyena, but it is not a wolf.
fact: Aardwolves eat mostly termites, and one can lick up thousands of them in a single night.
fact: An adaptation is a body part or behaviour that helps an animal survive where it lives.
fact: «Aardwolf» is a noun: an aardwolf, two aardwolves.
exercise: «The aardwolf is a small hyena that eats mostly termites.» What does the aardwolf eat most? | Mice and birds | *Termites | Fish from rivers | Fallen apples
exercise: Which body part helps an aardwolf catch termites each night? | A long curly tail | Thick, short claws | *A long sticky tongue | Big, flat ears
exercise: The aardwolf is related to which animal? | Elephants | Zebras | Termites | *Hyenas
test: Where do aardwolves live? | Australia | *Southern and eastern Africa | South America | Northern Europe
test: What does a context clue do? | It hides the meaning of the word from the reader | *It gives hints about a word's meaning from the words around it | It only works in maths lessons | It is always a picture in the book
exam: What does an aardwolf do each night? | It sleeps in trees all day | *It licks up thousands of termites with its long sticky tongue | It hunts large zebras | It builds nests from dry grass
